  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Structure
    
    A fractured trade terrace on Aurora Stack's southern face, built in three tiers of aurora-crystal scaffolding during the Great Thaw for crystal commerce. The original E'frostling construction remains elegant where it survives. Much of it does not survive. The middle gallery bears char-black glass streaks from the Vum∴tenebra — a fire-and-light war between the ☽'shadow Covens' Order and the E'frostlings, Aurora Stack's merchant-class faction. The southern spires, cracked during the Breach, still weep mineral runoff in spring-thaw. A corruption scar left by the casting of the Grulkzul Omega Strike — an unauthorized fusion of Nightshelf fire-knowledge and blood-working performed during the Orca Incursion — spreads from where the Omega Obelisk once stood and has not been cleansed. Corruption blooms seasonally in the deepest corners, spreading like frostbite through the ice itself. The merchants work around it.
    
    ## Contested History
    
    Momiou has changed hands three times. The sequence matters because it is routinely misremembered.
    
    | Period | Controlling Faction | Circumstances |
    |---|---|---|
    | Construction through pre-Thaw era | E'frostlings | Original builders; wards predating the Great Thaw |
    | Vum∴tenebra | ☽'shadow Covens' Order | Augurs used the ☽'glacial Crystalline Spiral to read frozen memory-scars in E'frostling defensive ice, identifying structural weaknesses the E'frostlings could not parse. Seventeen E'frostlings killed. Entire corridors frozen mid-collapse; flooding claimed the lower retreat chambers. Crystal stockpiles destroyed in the fighting rendered the Flipper Accord inoperable |
    | Post–Abyss Collapse Tide | E'frostlings | Reclaimed the terrace after the Abyss Collapse Tide devastated the Order's lower galleries |
    | Orca Incursion–present | ☽'shadow Covens' Order | Retaken during the Incursion; current holders, though E'frostlings and splinter faction Qingqe'frostlings maintain trade presence |
    
    The Flipper Accord's collapse after the Vum∴tenebra produced seven renegotiations, with casualties at each round. The ice in the middle gallery still holds frozen recursions of those killed by Crystalline Spiral practitioners — their last thoughts preserved, cycling through centuries of cold. The Absconditu Verses, a scriptural codification of the Mandatum∴absconditu doctrine of strategic hiddenness, were later recovered from ice-scorings in the collapsed gallery, transcribed by an unknown hand.
    
    The Breach — an orca-linked conflagration sparked by the Qingqe'frostlings' attempt to claim the Compass of Crystal by force — burned at the terrace for what the chronicles say was three cycles. During the Shattered-Spire Assault, E'frostling warehouses were destroyed and the southern crystal reserves shattered by sympathetic vibration; a crystal register storing Midnight Claws operative rosters was among the losses.
    
    ## Notable Features
    
    The **Compass of Crystal**, a navigation artifact originally crafted by Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam during the Great Thaw, sits in a vault beneath the eastern spire, sealed by three factions' authentication marks. Below the vault lies a deeper gallery where the Covens sealed an experimental fire-core that fused aurora-light with captured flame and developed what the sources describe as hunger. Fourteen fire-keepers died containing it. Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss, founder of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, died confronting what her order had created; her sacrifice diminished the corruption but did not end it.
    
    Memorial stones at the frozen edge bear names local archivists recognize but no one visits.
    
    ## Current State
    
    Momiou thrives — merchant caravans and fire-core runners cross daily — because it has to. Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam still walks the terraces some mornings, though she has held no authority here in generations. The locals call her "the ghost who owns nothing" and set aside the best fire-core shipments for her.
    
    During Long Darks, those passing through the terrace report the thin veil manifesting as replays: sounds of battle, transparent figures holding positions long since overrun. The locals call Momiou "the Terrace That Holds Its Breath." When the aurora dims and the wind rises, the ice produces a low sound that is not the clean song of living crystal. Certain other sounds make survivors of Momiou go still and quiet, even generations later.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771578689214_0", anchor: "Seventeen E'frostlings killed", text: "Sixteen. I have now written this number four times across three entries because the ice says sixteen and every source above the ice says seventeen. See my annotation on the ☽'shadow Covens' Order entry. One body's worth of discrepancy, recurring with a regularity that has moved past coincidence into something I lack a word for. I considered silently correcting the main text. I did not. The seventeen belongs to the chronicle tradition; the sixteen belongs to the ice. This apparatus exists precisely so that both can stand and the reader can see the seam.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578689214_1", anchor: "Construction through pre-Thaw era", text: "The table contradicts the opening paragraph and the E'frostlings entry itself, which places the faction's rise during the Great Thaw, not before it. The 'wards predating the Great Thaw' are real — I have seen them in the scaffolding ice — but they are not E'frostling work. Someone built here first. I left the ambiguity in the table because I cannot yet identify who, and dating construction ice by aurora-saturation alone is imprecise enough that I will not speculate in print. But someone should walk down there with proper instruments before the transition makes it irrelevant.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578689214_2", anchor: "an unauthorized fusion of Nightshelf fire-knowledge and blood-working", text: "'Unauthorized.' The fire-knowledge component required Keeper training. Someone trained them. Institutions that disavow operations after the fact are not the same as institutions that never ordered them.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578689214_3", anchor: "the ghost who owns nothing", text: "She owns a compass in a vault beneath her feet and a counter-charter filed the same season as the Long-dark Edict. The locals are being kind. They are not wrong.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578689214_4", anchor: "names local archivists recognize but no one visits", text: "I recognize three of them from depth-stratum requisition slips. Supply clerks. Not the sort of names that earn visits.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
